 "splits": {
  "35": [
   {
    "text": "Did you have any luck?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "No. But that's not really the point.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "47": [
   {
    "text": "I gotta go, gotta go.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "In beautiful British Columbia-- Scully?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "61": [
   {
    "text": "So they have already gotten to you.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "How did you know how to contact me?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "70": [
   {
    "text": "...so that you wouldn't remember me.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "Look, what is this all about?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "97": [
   {
    "text": "Do you even know me?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "Can we talk about this over dinner? Please?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "118": [
   {
    "text": "Skulls, look, I can prove it.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "Hey. I'm armed.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "138": [
   {
    "text": "It's the Mandela Effect.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "What do you mean?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "172": [
   {
    "text": "The what effect?",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "The Mandela Effect.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "192": [
   {
    "text": "Damn it, it's still wrong!",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "Easy, easy.",
    "speaker": "Shop Owner"
   }
  ],
  "227": [
   {
    "text": "It's the Mengele Effect.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "It's the Mengele Effect, just say it.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   }
  ],
  "240": [
   {
    "text": "I never mentioned a hypno-ray gun.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "It's faulty memory because Occam's razor.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   }
  ],
  "277": [
   {
    "text": "Well, a conspiracy nut is right twice a day.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "No, that's a broken clock.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   }
  ],
  "279": [
   {
    "text": "...so you will ignore the ones that are true.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "Reggie, take it from a fellow nut, okay?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "324": [
   {
    "text": "Now you're just--",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "What?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "325": [
   {
    "text": "You're just embarrassing yourself at this point.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   },
   {
    "text": "Those were the official reasons.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "336": [
   {
    "text": "What's that?",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Prime minister of Grenada...",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   }
  ],
  "479": [
   {
    "text": "What do you mean?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "No one can tell the difference anymore...",
    "speaker": "Dr. They"
   }
  ],
  "480": [
   {
    "text": "...between what's real and what's fake.",
    "speaker": "Dr. They"
   },
   {
    "text": "There's still objective truth, objective reality.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "488": [
   {
    "text": "It was George Orwell that said that.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "Well, for now maybe.",
    "speaker": "Dr. They"
   }
  ],
  "491": [
   {
    "text": "They won't know whether to believe it or not.",
    "speaker": "Dr. They"
   },
   {
    "text": "To be honest, I'm not believing any of this.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "498": [
   {
    "text": "All you really need is a laptop.",
    "speaker": "Dr. They"
   },
   {
    "text": "So that's what this has all been about?",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "539": [
   {
    "text": "Yeah, you did, I've heard this before.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "It was 35 years ago about...",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "540": [
   {
    "text": "...on the banks of Mogoagogo River.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   },
   {
    "text": "On the banks of Mogoagogo River.",
    "speaker": "Reggie"
   }
  ],
  "608": [
   {
    "text": "There'll always be more X-Files.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "No.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ],
  "635": [
   {
    "text": "I see you found your lost episode.",
    "speaker": "Dana Scully"
   },
   {
    "text": "Turns out it wasn't a Twilight Zone.",
    "speaker": "Fox Mulder"
   }
  ]
 },
 "text": {
  "42": "I think you just like saying \"squatching.\" Are we still on for dinner tomorrow night?",
  "63": "I-- It had to be someplace safe.",
  "76": "The first Twilight Zone episode you ever saw, it was \"The Lost Martian,\" right?",
  "107": "Wait, what? Oh, now I get it.",
  "157": "So who are you?\nI think my name is Reggie.",
  "165": "...is one of the fondest memories I have.",
  "169": "...was spelled different than how I remembered. Not with two S's, but with two Z's.",
  "228": "--is simply people misremembering stuff.",
  "233": "...if not identical, then very similar universe. So people's memories are correct...",
  "239": "It's a lot better than some evil entity zapping people's brains with a hypno-ray gun.",
  "242": "Maybe in a parallel universe it is...",
  "243": "...but in still yet another universe, it's perhaps known as Occam's ax.",
  "252": "No \"Have a great summer,\" \"You were funny in math class.\" Nothing.",
  "283": "But there's no they there. Who is they?",
  "286": "This is a story of a man named They.",
  "288": "...to manipulate collective memory. Most people have never heard of him.",
  "292": "...involving future, one-way space flights beyond our realm...",
  "302": "...in a movie called Ka-Blaam.",
  "304": "...but rumors swirl that he was at the last presidential inauguration...",
  "306": "...he was seen occupying the last remaining seat available.",
  "412": "And the next thing you know, you're deep state.",
  "426": "...jumped on stage and started dancing like a spaz.",
  "429": "A coded message? Especially because the band's lead singer, the son of Hugh Everett III...",
  "473": "And no doubt, the kids will come up with some catchphrase for it.",
  "490": "...because it doesn't matter who knows about it.",
  "532": "Wait. Is that a wedding cake? Damn it!",
  "560": "When did that stop? Maybe it's another Mengele Effect. Right?",
  "588": "...beyond your solar system.",
  "592": "You're bringing drugs, you're bringing crime.",
  "605": "We're not alone in the universe...",
  "628": "We'll be sure to come visit you, Reggie.\nHeh. No, you won't.",
  "646": "I want to remember how it was."
 },
